# ===== INFRA (3) =====
# LT_USERNAME / LT_ACCESS_KEY stay placeholders locally on purpose: env.json:76-77 is still their
# source (not tokenised — env.json is parsed for every run and a local thor run must not be
# required to know LambdaTest credentials). CI supplies the real pair. secretScan allow-lists these.
LT_USERNAME=
LT_ACCESS_KEY=
# Was hardcoded as the fallback at capabilities.json:214; that literal is now removed, so this is
# the only source. Rotate in Applitools org settings and update this line.
APPLITOOLS_API_KEY=
# BSTACK_USERNAME / BSTACK_KEY were dropped along with the four dead bstack-* capability blocks in
# capabilities.json (no npm script ever referenced them; browserstack-local was removed from deps).
# Re-add them only together with a real BrowserStack capability block that reads them.
